  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Starting: In the first round, the holder of the 6-6 leads it. In subsequent rounds, the lead rotates.\n2. Matching: Players take turns adding a tile to either end of the line, matching the pips on the open ends.\n3. Passing: If a player cannot move, they must 'knock' (tap the table) and pass their turn.\n4. Ending: The round ends when a player goes 'domino' (empties their hand) or the game is 'blocked' (no one can move).",
    Player: "1. Starting: In the first round, the holder of the 6-6 leads it. In subsequent rounds, the lead rotates.\n2. Matching: Players take turns adding a tile to either end of the line, matching the pips on the open ends.\n3. Passing: If a player cannot move, they must 'knock' (tap the table) and pass their turn.\n4. Ending: The round ends when a player goes 'domino' (empties their hand) or the game is 'blocked' (no one can move).",
    objective: 'Be the first team to reach a cumulative score of 200 points.',
    gameplay: "1. Starting: In the first round, the holder of the 6-6 leads it. In subsequent rounds, the lead rotates.\n2. Matching: Players take turns adding a tile to either end of the line, matching the pips on the open ends.\n3. Passing: If a player cannot move, they must 'knock' (tap the table) and pass their turn.\n4. Ending: The round ends when a player goes 'domino' (empties their hand) or the game is 'blocked' (no one can move).",
    keyRules: [
      'Anti-clockwise rotation is the standard for play.',
      'Partners sit facing each other and are not allowed to show their tiles to one another.',
      "A 'Trout' (closing the ends so no one can move) is a key strategic maneuver.",
    ],
