    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first team to reach a cumulative score of 200 points.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. Starting: In the first round, the holder of the 6-6 leads it. In subsequent rounds, the lead rotates.\n2. Matching: Players take turns adding a tile to either end of the line, matching the pips on the open ends.\n3. Passing: If a player cannot move, they must 'knock' (tap the table) and pass their turn.\n4. Ending: The round ends when a player goes 'domino' (empties their hand) or the game is 'blocked' (no one can move).",
      "Scoring example: The winning team scores the total pip count of the losing team's remaining tiles. If the game is blocked, the team with fewer total pips wins the difference. Be the first team to reach a cumulative score of 200 points..",
